{% doc %}
  The short descriptive line under a product's name ("Decorative Wood Tray").

  Source is Shopify's STANDARD "Product subtitle" metafield,
  `descriptors.subtitle` — reserved by Shopify for exactly this ("stores a
  concise description of a product", 70 characters), so it is native rather
  than invented and any app or future theme reads the same field.

  Deliberately NOT product.type: the eight nav categories map one-to-one onto
  Type, so Type is what the category collections filter on. Reusing it here
  would print the category twice and couple the subtitle to merchandising.

  Renders nothing when the metafield is empty, so products without one simply
  keep a single-line card.

  @param {product} product - the product to read the subtitle from
  @param {string} [class] - class for the element
  @example
  {% render 'product-subtitle', product: product, class: 'product-card__subtitle' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- assign subtitle = product.metafields.descriptors.subtitle | metafield_text | strip -%}
{%- if subtitle != blank -%}
  <p class="{{ class | default: 'product-subtitle' }}">{{ subtitle }}</p>
{%- endif -%}
